  "script": {
    "segments": [
      {
        "narration": "Divers pulled crates of fake British pounds from this lake. Toplitz, in the Austrian Alps. A hundred and three metres deep, walled in by cliffs.",
        "visual_query": "austrian alpine lake steep cliffs",
        "visual_fallback": "alpine lake"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Nothing breathes below twenty metres down there. No oxygen, salty water, and a raft of sunken logs floating halfway to the bottom that blocks the way.",
        "visual_query": "styrian mountain lake dark water",
        "visual_fallback": "mountain lake"
      },
      {
        "narration": "So why keep diving it? Because in 1943 the Nazis ran a naval weapons range on that shore, detonating charges of four thousand kilos.",
        "visual_query": "austrian alps lake shoreline forest",
        "visual_fallback": "alpine shoreline"
      },
      {
        "narration": "A 1959 expedition brought up boxes of forged five-pound notes. One of the divers reported an aircraft lying somewhere below the logs.",
        "visual_query": "vintage 1950s diving expedition boat",
        "visual_fallback": "vintage diving"
      },
      {
        "narration": "The crates were Operation Bernhard, an SS plan to wreck Britain's economy with forgeries. Every expedition since has come back with paper. Never gold.",
        "visual_query": "old british pound banknotes closeup",
        "visual_fallback": "old banknotes"
      }
    ],
